<decompilertest>
<binaryimage arch="AARCH64:LE:64:v8A">
<!--
    Calls to the C11 Annex K bounds-checked functions keep every declared
    argument. P1 program prep, the built-in libc signatures
    (kuna-analysis protos/kuna_libcsigs.rs, no option).

    GCC loads a size passed twice into the later argument register and copies
    it into the earlier one (`mov x3,#64; mov w2,#0; mov x1,x3; bl memset_s`).
    Without a declaration, call recovery drops the later register because its
    value also reaches an earlier argument, so the call printed
    `memset_s(v1,0x40,0)`. The script loads boundschecked_aarch64_{le,be}.so
    and boundschecked_thumb.so (sources and recipes in the fixtures README),
    whose callers mirror GCC 15 -O2 -fPIC output.

    Assert #1: memset_s keeps its count (AArch64 both byte orders, Thumb).
    Assert #2: memcpy_s keeps its count, and on Thumb gains no fifth argument
    from the pushed r3 slot.
    Assert #3: memmove_s, strncpy_s and strncat_s keep their counts.
    Assert #4: sprintf_s prints its format string and the two values.
-->
  <bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x1000" readonly="true">c0035fd6</bytechunk>
  <symbol space="ram" offset="0x1000" name="harness_stub"/>
</binaryimage>
